    "created_at": "2018-03-20T13:50:19Z",
    "updated_at": "2018-03-20T13:50:19Z",
    "body": "So thinking about this in light of the tests at `shadow-dom/event-post-dispatch.html` it seems this is still not entirely correct. With the patch is proposed, you can observe whether an event started out in a shadow tree or not.\r\n\r\nI think _clearTargets_ should instead be based on event's path. You find the last tuple in event's path with a non-null target. And then if that tuple contains a node inside a shadow tree in one of the three target fields, you set _clearTargets_ to true.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
